---
// Privacy notice. DRAFT FOR OWNER REVIEW: covers the waitlist form (Tally), the
// entry form (Tally), payments by bank transfer and emails sent to us. It must be
// reviewed before entries open (Malaysia's PDPA; entrants may be under 18).
// Change DATES.privacyUpdated in src/site.ts whenever the wording changes.
import Base from '../layouts/Base.astro';
import Hero from '../components/Hero.astro';
import SiteFooter from '../components/SiteFooter.astro';
import { SITE_NAME, CONTACT_EMAIL, INSTAGRAM_HANDLE, INSTAGRAM_URL, SOUP_KITCHEN_NAME, DATES, formatDate, WAITLIST_FORM_URL } from '../site';

const intro = `What ${SITE_NAME} collects about you, and what we do with it.`;
---

<Base title="Privacy" description={intro}>
  <Hero padBottom={[110, 150]}>
    <h1 class="t-display-xl privacy-title">Privacy</h1>
    <p slot="aside" class="t-lead">{intro}</p>
  </Hero>

  <main id="main" class="privacy">
    <div class="placeholder-card privacy__draft">
      <span class="pill">Draft</span>
      <p>This notice is a draft and is waiting for review. Last updated {formatDate(DATES.privacyUpdated)}.</p>
    </div>

    <section>
      <h2 class="t-heading">Who we are</h2>
      <p>
        {SITE_NAME} is an essay competition run by student volunteers. If you have a question about your data, email{' '}
        <a href={`mailto:${CONTACT_EMAIL}`}>{CONTACT_EMAIL}</a>.
      </p>
    </section>

    <section>
      <h2 class="t-heading">What this website collects</h2>
      <p>
        The site has no accounts, no analytics, no advertising and no tracking cookies. Our fonts are served from our
        own site, not from another company. The one exception is the waitlist form on the Home and Competition pages,
        which is run by Tally (see "The waitlist" below). The entry form, when entries are open, is also run by Tally (see "The entry form" below).
      </p>
      <p>
        Our host, Firebase Hosting (run by Google), processes basic technical information such as your IP address so
        it can deliver the pages and keep the site secure. We don't use that information ourselves.
      </p>
    </section>

    <section>
      <h2 class="t-heading">If you email us</h2>
      <p>
        We receive your email address and whatever you write. We use it only to reply to you, and we don't share it.
        We delete it 12 months after our last reply.
      </p>
    </section>

    <section>
      <h2 class="t-heading">Instagram</h2>
      <p>If you follow or message us on Instagram, Instagram's own privacy policy applies to what you share there.</p>
    </section>

    <section>
      <h2 class="t-heading">The waitlist</h2>
      <p>
        If you join the waitlist, we collect your email address and your tick to say you agree to us emailing you.
        Nothing else.
      </p>
      <p>
        The form is run by Tally (tally.so), which stores what you submit for us. See{' '}
        <a href="https://tally.so/help/privacy-policy" rel="noopener noreferrer">Tally's privacy policy</a>. On the
        pages that show the form, your browser loads Tally's form and script from tally.so, so Tally can see technical
        details such as your IP address, as its policy explains. If the form doesn't load, we show a plain link to it
        at <a href={WAITLIST_FORM_URL} rel="noopener noreferrer">{WAITLIST_FORM_URL}</a>.
      </p>
      <p>
        We use your email only to email you once, when entries open. We delete it when entries close. To come off the
        list sooner, email <a href={`mailto:${CONTACT_EMAIL}`}>{CONTACT_EMAIL}</a>.
      </p>
    </section>

    <section>
      <h2 class="t-heading">If you are under 18 and join the waitlist</h2>
      <p>
        Many entrants will be under 18. For the waitlist we collect only an email address. If you are under 18, please
        make sure a parent or guardian knows you are signing up. A parent or guardian can ask us at any time to delete
        their child's email address: email <a href={`mailto:${CONTACT_EMAIL}`}>{CONTACT_EMAIL}</a>.
      </p>
    </section>

    <section>
      <h2 class="t-heading">The entry form</h2>
      <p>When you enter, the entry form collects:</p>
      <ul>
        <li>your full name, email and country;</li>
        <li>your school (optional) and your age;</li>
        <li>the prompt you chose and your essay (a PDF);</li>
        <li>your fee choice and, if you have one, your fee support code;</li>
        <li>a screenshot of your payment, the transfer reference and the name on the account you paid from;</li>
        <li>if you are under 18, a second email address (we suggest a parent or guardian's).</li>
      </ul>
      <p>
        The form is run by Tally (tally.so), which stores the responses for us. Tally says it stores form data on servers
        in the European Union. See <a href="https://tally.so/help/privacy-policy" rel="noopener noreferrer">Tally's privacy policy</a>
        for the details. On the page that shows the form, your browser loads Tally's form and script from tally.so, so
        Tally can see technical details such as your IP address, as its policy explains.
      </p>
    </section>

    <section>
      <h2 class="t-heading">Payments</h2>
      <p>
        You pay the entry fee by bank transfer, directly to {SOUP_KITCHEN_NAME}'s bank account. {SITE_NAME} never handles the
        money. {SOUP_KITCHEN_NAME} shares a list of incoming transfers (date, amount and reference) with us, so we can match
        each payment to an entry.
      </p>
    </section>

    <section>
      <h2 class="t-heading">If you are shortlisted or win</h2>
      <p>
        If you are shortlisted or win, your name only (not your school, country or age) may be published on this website and
        on Instagram (<a href={INSTAGRAM_URL} rel="noopener noreferrer">{INSTAGRAM_HANDLE}</a>). These names stay published
        after the competition ends.
      </p>
    </section>

    <section>
      <h2 class="t-heading">If you are under 18 and enter</h2>
      <p>
        A parent or guardian must agree to you entering and to us handling your details. We may email the second email
        address on your entry to ask about this.
      </p>
    </section>

    <section>
      <h2 class="t-heading">How long we keep entry data</h2>
      <p>
        By {formatDate(DATES.entryDataDeleted)} we delete the entry data we no longer need: emails, ages, essays, payment
        screenshots and fee support emails. We keep the published names of shortlisted entrants and winners, and the
        certificate records.
      </p>
    </section>

    <section>
      <h2 class="t-heading">Certificates and publishing names</h2>
      <p>
        Each certificate has a code. You can check a code on our <a href="/verify/">Verify page</a>, which shows the
        name, award, edition and issue date on that certificate. A code you type into the box is checked in your
        browser and is not sent anywhere. If you open a link that already has the code in it, the code is part of the
        page address, so our host (Firebase Hosting) receives it like any other address. Certificate details are
        stored in the site in locked form, so there is no public list of names: they open only for someone who has
        the code.
      </p>
      <p>
        We may publish the names of shortlisted entrants and winners on this site and on Instagram, as set out
        above. Entrants agree to this on the entry form.
      </p>
    </section>

    <section>
      <h2 class="t-heading">Your rights</h2>
      <p>
        Under Malaysia's Personal Data Protection Act, you can ask what personal data we hold about you, ask us to
        correct it, and withdraw your consent to us using it. Email{' '}
        <a href={`mailto:${CONTACT_EMAIL}`}>{CONTACT_EMAIL}</a> and we'll reply.
      </p>
    </section>
  </main>

  <SiteFooter />
</Base>

<style>
  .privacy-title { margin-top: 64px; }

  .privacy {
    padding: 44px var(--gutter) 24px;
    display: flex;
    flex-direction: column;
    gap: 40px;
    font-size: var(--fs-body-lg);
    line-height: var(--lh-body-lg);
  }
  .privacy section { display: flex; flex-direction: column; gap: 14px; max-width: 680px; }
  .privacy p { text-wrap: pretty; }
  .privacy ul { padding-left: 1.25em; display: flex; flex-direction: column; gap: 6px; }
  .privacy a { font-weight: 600; overflow-wrap: anywhere; }
  .privacy__draft { max-width: 680px; }

  @media (min-width: 960px) {
    .privacy-title { margin-top: 110px; }
    .privacy { padding: 96px var(--gutter) 24px; gap: 56px; }
    .privacy section { gap: 18px; }
  }
</style>
